From fa4d0bf7b86d5b61cd1c20542584b2af918e7f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:29:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: qcom-spmi: support the fixed-range PM8226 APC rail

Retain the boot FTS2 range and immutable selector grid, CPU0 SAW ownership,
confirmed old-voltage recovery before returning an error to OPP/genpd,
and safe PWM if only AUTO mode restoration fails. Keep the fixed leader
always on and preserve legacy regulator operation tables per instance.

Port the qualified complete CPU regulator component onto fresh official
for-next a2a6f6b0b394. Preserve the newer allocator APIs and the private
raw-spinlock MMIO mapping added by Dmitry Baryshkov's 053c50a70525 fix.
Only the explicit MSM8226 L2 master uses the permanent map published by
its SPM owner; return probe-defer until that map exists. No new register
map is created for that owner and legacy maps remain per-device.

The actual acquisition helper passes 47 cases/407 checks with four failing
controls. Three actual FTS2/provider/recovery models pass with normal
address/undefined/leak sanitizers. ARM/ARM64 PREEMPT_RT builds compile 10
related objects with W=1 and no diagnostics. The L2 owner and PMIC parent
raw-lock fixes are separate prerequisites; physical voltage, RT/lockdep,
CPU stress and deep-PM acceptance remain pending.

Composite port of Timothy Schmidt's later CPU component from
790c9c5407e17ad1d2395c2ec4bdfcfc8dc82826. Original author/date retained.
Codex generated the current-base mapping split, API port, changelog and
qualification. Human DCO remains pending; no Signed-off-by is added.
